resolve_external: a guest that bundles SQLite binds to its own copy, not macOS's

Same rule the loader already applies to Apple's private crypto dylibs: when the
global dlsym answers an import from /usr/lib/libsqlite3.dylib and a loaded guest
ELF defines the symbol, bind to the guest's definition (fall back to the host
only when no guest provides it). MACAPK_GUEST_SQLITE=0 restores the old binding.

Measured on Instagram 455 (macOS 27.2). libstartup.so defines the whole sqlite3_*
API; libscrollmerged.so imports it and was bound to macOS's libsqlite3:

  * sqlite3_config is variadic. Bionic passes variadic args in registers, Apple's
    arm64 ABI reads them from the stack, so the host stored a stack word
    (0x70422f8c28) as the SQLITE_CONFIG_LOG callback. The first sqlite3_log --
    a WAL recovery inside sqlite3_exec (walIndexReadHdr) -- jumped to it:
    SIGILL on SWPool3, breakpad abort, about a minute into a logged-in session.
  * Two SQLite engines then share the same database, -wal and -shm files with
    different locking and WAL-index code.

After the patch every sqlite3_* import of libscrollmerged.so resolves to
libstartup.so ("-> guest libstartup.so (preferred over macOS libsqlite3)").

Applies to vendor/macapk at 57c9912 (after 0005, 0006) with `patch -p1` from
vendor/macapk.

diff --git a/runtime/translator/src/arm64_native.cpp b/runtime/translator/src/arm64_native.cpp
index f2e974b..a17ceaf 100644
--- a/runtime/translator/src/arm64_native.cpp
+++ b/runtime/translator/src/arm64_native.cpp
@@ -2409,6 +2421,27 @@ static bool host_dylib_is_private_crypto(void* addr) {
         || std::strncmp(base, "libssl", 6) == 0;
 }
 
+// True when a host symbol pointer lives in macOS's /usr/lib/libsqlite3.dylib.
+// Same reasoning as the private-crypto case: an app that BUNDLES its own SQLite
+// (Instagram's libstartup.so defines the whole sqlite3_* API) must not have
+// some of its libraries bound to Apple's copy. MEASURED on Instagram 455:
+// libscrollmerged.so imports sqlite3_exec/sqlite3_config, they resolved to the
+// host dylib, and two failures followed --
+//   * sqlite3_config is VARIADIC: Bionic passes the variadic args in registers,
+//     Apple's arm64 ABI reads them from the stack, so the host stored a stack
+//     word (0x70422f8c28) as the SQLITE_CONFIG_LOG callback; the first
+//     sqlite3_log (a WAL recovery inside sqlite3_exec) jumped to it: SIGILL on
+//     SWPool3, breakpad abort, about a minute into a logged-in session;
+//   * two SQLite engines then share the same database, -wal and -shm files
+//     with different locking and WAL-index code.
+static bool host_dylib_is_sqlite(void* addr) {
+    Dl_info di;
+    if (!addr || !dladdr(addr, &di) || !di.dli_fname) return false;
+    const char* slash = std::strrchr(di.dli_fname, '/');
+    const char* base = slash ? slash + 1 : di.dli_fname;
+    return std::strncmp(base, "libsqlite3", 10) == 0;
+}
+
 // True when `addr` is owned by a Cocoa framework bundle (.../Foo.framework/...).
 // A framework export can never satisfy an Android ELF import: those are
 // ObjC/Swift app-facing implementations, not a Bionic substitute, and dlsym
@@ -2914,7 +2947,13 @@ void* Image::resolve_external(const std::string& name, uint8_t bind) {
                 }
             }
         }
-        if (host_dylib_is_private_crypto(p)) {
+        const bool host_crypto = host_dylib_is_private_crypto(p);
+        static const bool kGuestSqlite = [] {
+            const char* e = std::getenv("MACAPK_GUEST_SQLITE");   // =0: legacy host binding
+            return !(e && e[0] == '0');
+        }();
+        const bool host_sqlite = !host_crypto && kGuestSqlite && host_dylib_is_sqlite(p);
+        if (host_crypto || host_sqlite) {
             for (Image* img : loaded_images()) {
                 if (img == this) continue;
                 if (void* g = img->lookup(name.c_str())) {
@@ -2922,8 +2961,10 @@ void* Image::resolve_external(const std::string& name, uint8_t bind) {
                     if (n_guest.fetch_add(1) < 128)
                         std::fprintf(stderr,
                             "[arm64-native] %s: '%s' -> guest %s (preferred "
-                            "over Apple's private crypto dylib)\n",
-                            dbg_name_, name.c_str(), img->name());
+                            "over %s)\n",
+                            dbg_name_, name.c_str(), img->name(),
+                            host_crypto ? "Apple's private crypto dylib"
+                                        : "macOS libsqlite3");
                     return g;
                 }
             }
